The MIT license covers these files individually. A combined work that
incorporates AGPL-covered HarnessMinimizer code must comply with the AGPL unless
covered by a separate commercial agreement. The MIT license do not relicense
the HarnessMinimizer code or third-party components used by these files.

1. Third-party components and benchmark materials
-----------------------------------------------

Upstream copyright notices, permissions, and license conditions remain
applicable to third-party components under either HarnessMinimizer licensing
option. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/ for component details.

LLVM material retains Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception terms. Upstream treereduce
material retains its MIT terms. Separately obtained Perses engines retain
their GPL-3.0-or-later terms.

The MIT grant for evaluation code does not cover target libraries, or other
upstream materials in benchmark/. Their applicable permissions and notices
remain in effect. Other tools and packages downloaded by the Dockerfile or
installers retain their own license terms.
